The function already compiles to a single inlined field-store, and any alternative (e.g. calling the lower-level `SetField` directly) is either identical after inlining or risks a signature/access mismatch, so I kept the exact same call.

```cpp
    void SetSensorType(FIT_SENSOR_TYPE sensorType)
    {
        SetFieldENUMValue(0, sensorType, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```